export const networkGraphReference = `Network graph rules: use networkGraph for data-driven relationships across entities already present in the Power BI/HyperPBI dataset. Use entities + relationships only; never use legacy sourceField/targetField edge-table mode and do not create or require a separate edge table. Each entity requires an id and supplied Field Manifest alias; labelField, color, symbol, and nodeSize are optional. Each relationship connects entity IDs; branchLabel may add a presentation-only grouping node. Power BI model relationships determine which values arrive together and HyperPBI deduplicates flattened combinations. Any number of entity definitions and relationship depths are supported within maxNodes. Prefer hybrid for operational trees, hierarchical for deterministic levels, force only for explicit free-form exploration, and circular for peer networks. Use focusMode:"none" unless adjacency dimming is explicitly requested. Node tooltips default on and display only the complete human label; edge tooltips default off. Prefer wrapped labels and autoCompact for dense hierarchy levels; initialZoom can override automatic zoom. Explicit colors should distinguish entity types. Directed arrows are independent of tooltip settings. Node clicks preserve field and Power BI row lineage. Use mermaidDiagram instead when the user supplies Mermaid source or requests an authored flowchart, sequence, class, state, ER, architecture, or documentation diagram. Never invent fields, joins, callbacks, or network sources.`;
